<WRAP center round important 60%>Due to lack of Hardware NAT support (as of Barrier Breaker), although all the physical ports are gigabit speeds, the WAN-LAN throughput is only capable of ~100Mbps speed (this only affects you if you have greater than this available from your ISP).

[[https://dev.openwrt.org/ticket/11779|WDR4300 - hardware nat feature]] is for a different switch, but comments explain the reason (see also abnoxious forum post [[https://forum.openwrt.org/viewtopic.php?id=60033|No Hardware NAT Support = No FUN]].</WRAP>

